  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nUpper trough along the east coast will gradually move east as high \npressure takes hold across our region, with a period of dry, and \ngradually warming temperatures as we head into Friday. Highs Friday \nshould generally top out in the mid to upper 80s across much of the \nlowlands, but overall, humidity should remain low, providing for \npleasant weather. River valley fog will be possible in the mornings \nduring this period. \n\n\nUpper ridge will start to break down over the weekend with the \napproach of a system and associated frontal boundary from the north. \nThis will bring a return of unsettled weather to the region. \nSouthwesterly flow on Saturday out ahead of the approaching system \nwill result in continued warm, and slightly more humid conditions as \nof late. Aforementioned front should generally sag south of the area \neither Sunday or Monday, with a period of dry conditions taking hold \nagain for the start of next week.",
